628 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 441 0 R
/E (Muyamuri/Umsizi is a comprehensive, AI-powered digital platform that transforms citizen-government interaction across emergency response, municipal services, agricultural support, and official government communication. Leveraging WhatsApp's ubiquitous presence in Zimbabwe, with over 12.83 million active internet subscriptions, the platform creates a seamless interface that receives citizen reports while proactively communicating official government positions with verifiable citations. At its core is a custom Large Language Model with Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) technology, fine-tuned on Zimbabwean government documents and policies. The solution is currently at Proof-of-Concept stage with all core functionality operational, including WhatsApp integration, NLP processing, multimodal data ingestion \(text, image, audio, video, location, documents\), and secure Vector & MongoDB storage. The platform has already demonstrated its capability to scrape and process data from Zimpapers publications, proving the viability of building comprehensive Shona and Ndebele language corpora for truly indigenous AI.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
629 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 441 0 R
/E (The solution extends beyond a chatbot to establish a sovereign data foundation through Project Zvipo, systematically aggregating public government data, documenting indigenous tree knowledge, and curating local language datasets, creating the data infrastructure upon which Zimbabwe's AI future will be built. The proposal spans all four AI4I tracks: Development \(primary\), with a working prototype and clear implementation roadmap; Data, through comprehensive data collection, governance, and curation; Design, with user-centred dashboards currently in development for various stakeholders; and Deployment, addressing responsible AI governance, bias testing, security controls, and Data Protection Act compliance. With all core technical components operational and the remaining dashboard development well-defined, Muyamuri/Umsizi is deployment-ready and capable of delivering measurable public value within weeks of approval. This solution embodies the National AI Strategy's vision that "AI must carry Zimbabwean fingerprints and create Zimbabwean opportunities," contributing to digital sovereignty, inclusive growth, and improved service delivery for all citizens.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
