/E (Matts was born in Harare and went to Chirodzo Primary School and Harare High School where he was the Headboy \(School Captain\). In 1978 he completed a Bachelor of Accountancy \(Hons\) degree at the University of Zimbabwe. He studied for Articles with KPMG from December 1980, where he qualified as a Chartered Accountant and was admitted as a member of the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Zimbabwe \(ICAZ\) in January 1984. He completed his Masters of Business Administration \(MBA\) degree, specialising in Finance at the University of Delaware, USA in 1986. He worked for KPMG's London office from 1986 to 1990 when he returned home. He also did an MSc in Strategic Management with the University of Derby \(UK\). He was Finance Director for Chibuku, Operations Director for OK Zimbabwe and Group CEO of Zimpapers before joining Reserve Bank of Zimbabwe as Division Chief: Corporate Governance, Risk Management and Internal Audit. In May 2011 to December 2018 he joined the Institute of Chartered Accountants as the Chief Executive Officer of his professional regulatory body for the second time 11 years after his first appointment. He was charged with leading and directing the Secretariat to deliver service and value to members and other stakeholders. He is a holder of a PhD in Management from Christ University, India. He also has a Certificate in Ministry Essentials Training Program from the Pan African Christian College \(PACC\). He has sat on a number of Boards including being a Council Member ofthe National Manpower Advisory \(NAMACO\); Zimbabwe Council for Higher Education \(ZIMCHE\); Council Member of Bindura University of Science Education; Member of ZIMDEF Audit Committee and Member of MEFMI Audit Committee and currently is the Board Chairperson of the Zimbabwe Women's Microfinance Bank and Deputy Chairman of POTRAZ. He is Past President of the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Zimbabwe, Zimbabwe Association of Accounting Technicians \(ZAAT\) and the Institute ofInternal Auditors of Zimbabwe \(IIAZ\). He was the inaugural Chairperson of Zimbabwe Women Microfinance Bank \(ZWMB\) for 6 years to December 2023. He was the Deputy Chair of POTRAZ Boardand is the Acting Chairperson of the Audit Office inaugural Board. He was Board member of ZIMCHE and Bindura University of Science and Technology Council including being Chairperson \(BUSE\). Matts Kunaka was Megafest's Zimbabwe Director of the Year for 2016. Matts has three other Masters degrees being; MBA from the University of Delaware, USA; an MSc in Big Data Analytics from Chinhoyi University of Technology and an MPhil from Christ University, India where he obtained his PhD in Management. He is a Partner at KRES Chartered Accountants \(a member firm of REANDA INTERNATIONAL\) and also lectures at Catholic University of Zimbabwe where he obtained a Post Graduate Diploma in Education in 2022. In addition to being a CA\(Z\) he is also a CA \(SA\). A devout Christian, Matts is married to Kuda and has five children and seven grand children. He loves golf, karate and flying.)
/Pg 107 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
