28829 0 obj
<<
/Title (Zimbabwe's agricultural sector faces mounting pressures that existing extension systems, both private and government-led, are ill-equipped to handle, lacking the capacity to collect, integrate, and synthesise data for timely interventions. Critical gaps persist across three areas; animal invasion reporting, farm crop protection, and disease and pest surveillance. Without AI-powered tools or spatial analytics to identify prevalence patterns and disease spread, farmers remain vulnerable, authorities lack targeted intervention capabilities, and insights remain trapped in isolated information silos rather than accessible to all stakeholders, from government agencies and National Parks to private agribusinesses and research institutions.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 28749 0 R
